From f308b73307b2f49effef2c91034358ecd8fac63c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 06:00:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 14/28] test: replace TEST_PARAMS with test variants

wallet_txn_doublespend.py and wallet_txn_clone.py now declare their
--mineblock runs as a "mineblock" variant. That was the last
TEST_PARAMS entry, so test_runner.py drops TEST_PARAMS, its existence
check and the expansion code: the runner runs a test's variants from
the test's own class ("<file>" for the first, "<file>[<variant>]"
for the others).

The three commented-out FIXME entries (descriptors runs of rpc_psbt.py,
wallet_basic.py and wallet_keypool.py, which fail) move to comments on
those tests' classes.

The full functional suite runs the same tests with the same results.
---
 test/functional/rpc_psbt.py               |  2 +
 test/functional/test_runner.py            | 90 ++++++++++-------------
 test/functional/timing.json               |  4 +-
 test/functional/wallet_basic.py           |  2 +
 test/functional/wallet_keypool.py         |  2 +
 test/functional/wallet_txn_clone.py       |  2 +
 test/functional/wallet_txn_doublespend.py |  2 +
 7 files changed, 52 insertions(+), 52 deletions(-)

